# Precision landing for the landing target (`just sim-landing`, docs/simulation.md), loaded after
# sat-teleop-copter.parm. Names, values and meanings are those of ArduPilot git
# fb773567896014da007bca58358704d4a0d8516f, libraries/AC_PrecLand/AC_PrecLand.cpp and
# AC_PrecLand_StateMachine.cpp: the same values real mode requires (docs/real-vehicle.md).
#
# On, with the MAVLink backend (type 1, "MAVLink" in the pinned source), which reads LANDING_TARGET.
PLND_ENABLED 1
PLND_TYPE 1
# A lost target: 1 is "Retry Landing (Normal Strictness)": descend for PLND_TIMEOUT, retry above where it
# was last seen, then (and when no target was ever seen) hold for FAILSAFE_INIT_TIMEOUT_MS, 7 s, and land
# vertically (AC_PrecLand_StateMachine.cpp, get_failsafe_actions). 2 would hold with no end.
PLND_STRICT 1
# No altitude window. check_target_status calls the target out of range, and so never lost, below
# PLND_ALT_MIN or above PLND_ALT_MAX or whenever there is no valid rangefinder (the simulation has
# none), and an out-of-range target is descended on whatever PLND_STRICT says. Zero for both
# disables the window.
PLND_ALT_MIN 0
PLND_ALT_MAX 0
# How old a sighting is when it reaches the autopilot. AC_PrecLand ignores the message's time stamp
# for this and matches each sighting with the inertial data PLND_LAG seconds back (default 0.02,
# range 0.02 to 0.25, reboot required: libraries/AC_PrecLand/AC_PrecLand.cpp, init and
# construct_pos_meas_using_rangefinder). The picture's measured age at the autopilot is about 0.06 s
# (docs/measurement.md, "Landing tag"), but a run at 0.06 landed 2.8 m from the tag and one at 0.15
# landed 0.01 m from it, so 0.15 stays until more runs say why.
PLND_LAG 0.15
